    <briefdescription>
<para>Result of a state evaluation (UpdateState_TPX / UpdateState_HPX). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>SI units: T [K], p [Pa], X [kg NaCl / kg fluid], H [J/kg], densities [kg/m^3], Cp [J/kg/K], Mu [Pa s], dRhodP [kg/m^3/Pa], dRhodT [kg/m^3/K], IsothermalCompressibility [1/Pa], IsobaricExpansivity [1/K]. Suffixes _l, _v, _h: the liquid, vapour and halite phase; a field of an absent phase is 0. Fields without a suffix are bulk values. A field that a model does not compute keeps its default (0, or 1 for Mu).</para>
<para>Single-phase states: the bulk fields are those of the phase.</para>
<para>Multiphase states (H2O-NaCl V+L, V+H, L+H, V+L+H; water two-phase), no change of values implied:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Rho, H: bulk values of the phase assemblage (H2O-NaCl: Rho = sum S_i Rho_i, H = sum S_i Rho_i H_i / Rho).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Cp: &quot;frozen&quot; bulk heat capacity sum S_i Rho_i Cp_i / Rho, with phase heat capacities at fixed phase composition. It contains no latent heat and is not dH/dT of the bulk state. 0 in V+L+H and in the two-phase states of the water models.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Mu is not a mixture viscosity; a multiphase model forms one from Mu_l, Mu_v and the saturations. In V+L, V+H and L+H it holds the default 1. In V+L+H and in the H-P-X V+L state at X = 0 it is S_l Mu_l + S_v Mu_v. In the two-phase states of the water models it is backend-specific (IAPWS-95: viscosity at T and bulk density).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>IsothermalCompressibility: in H2O-NaCl V+L, V+H and L+H the equilibrium derivative of the bulk density at fixed T and bulk X (the phases re-equilibrate), 0 in V+L+H and in the H-P-X V+L state at X = 0.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>IsobaricExpansivity, dRhodP, dRhodT: not computed for multiphase states (0; the IAPS-84 water model gives non-finite values in its two-phase states). </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
